or cars. The company was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Traverse City, Michigan. Hagerty, Inc. is a subsidiary of Hagerty Holding Corp.","ceo_bio":"Mr. McKeel O. Hagerty | Chairman & CEO | Age 58 | Compensation: $4.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $770K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $103K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Hagerty, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.7B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 32% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 23-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $194M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.47\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 27\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit 